From 811312d0d0971121fe742a361a57348ed581551c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 19:34:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Shrink the avatar picker grid, default every user to a real PixelBot

Two follow-ups from the avatar picker:

- The 5x5 seed grid used grid-cols-5 with aspect-square cells, which
  stretch to fill whatever width the parent panel happens to have —
  on a wide profile page that rendered each swatch nearly card-sized
  instead of a pick-one-from-a-grid thumbnail. Fixed to a real fixed
  36px swatch size (grid-cols-[repeat(5,36px)]), matching how a picker
  grid like this actually reads elsewhere (Slack's emoji/avatar
  pickers, etc).

- UserAvatar fell straight to the caller's plain initials for anyone
  who hadn't explicitly picked an avatar — which, right after this
  ships, is every user. Added defaultSeedForIdentifier (hashes a
  stable per-user identifier — email, or whopUserId if none — onto
  one of the same 25 curated seeds the picker grid already shows) so
  everyone gets a real, distinct-looking PixelBot by default instead
  of a blank initials circle. Initials are now a true last resort.
  The avatar picker pre-selects that same default seed/category when
  opened for a user who's never explicitly chosen, so what shows
  selected in the grid always matches what's actually showing as
  their avatar elsewhere, instead of contradicting it with an empty
  grid.

